{number: 114}
{title: Mine Eyes Have Seen the Glory}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Mine [C] eyes have seen the glory of the coming of the Lord;
He is [F] trampling out the vintage where the [C] grapes of wrath are stored;
He hath [C] loosed the fateful lightning of His [Am] terrible swift sword:
His [Dm] truth is [G7] marching [C] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Glory, glory, hallelujah!
[F] Glory, glory, halle-[C] lujah!
[C] Glory, glory, [Am] hallelujah!
His [Dm] truth is [G7] marching [C] on.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I have [C] seen Him in the watchfires of a hundred circling camps;
They have [F] builded Him an altar in the [C] evening dews and damps;
I can [C] read His righteous sentence by the [Am] dim and flaring lamps:
His [Dm] day is [G7] marching [C] on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In the [C] beauty of the lilies Christ was born across the sea,
With a [F] glory in His bosom that trans-[C] figures you and me:
As He [C] died to make men holy, let us [Am] live to make men free,
While [Dm] God is [G7] marching [C] on.
{end_of_verse}
